                <pb facs="0081" n="895" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg895"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On April 24, the United States introduced in the United Nations Disarmament
                    Commission a proposal on Essential Principles for a Disarmament Program. The
                    proposal was circulated as UN doc. DC/C.1/1. For text, see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Documents on Disarmament, 1945–1959</hi>, volume I,
                    pages 357–358. For statements made by Benjamin V. Cohen, Deputy United States
                    Representative on the Disarmament Commission, in Committee I of the Commission
                    regarding the proposal and the general United States position, see Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, May 12, 1952, pages 752–753. For
                    certain remarks <pb facs="0082" n="896" xml:id="pg896"/> by Cohen before
                    Committee II of the Commission on April 25, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid</hi>., pages 753–755.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
